  {
   "k": "1345498",
   "en": "The below is ⟦0⟧ player suggested strategies for ⟦1⟧. Bear in mind, due to the dynamic nature of the game, it may unfold differently for other players.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "qksxxt",
   "en": "Playing as ⟦0⟧ is slightly hard, the first problem that needs to be addressed is the player's almost total lack of industry. Although, it starts with one military factory, one tungsten and two units of coal.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "g5rlt7",
   "en": "Apart that its population is smaller, but unlike ⟦0⟧, ⟦1⟧ takes the advantage of the opportunity to start with a better territory and a slightly bigger army.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "1ebp7oy",
   "en": "Pick \"Develop Ningxia\" as the first focus. Immediately rush it down until you get everything necessary to produce and build anything. Your goal will be to declare and unite all of the Ma nations as soon as possible, even sooner depending if ⟦0⟧ decides to go with its fascist branch or not. Take \"Strengthening Our Position\" and go for opposition, in order to go down and produce and get more manpower out of it. Pick \"Strike at the Traitors\" instead of \"Demand Submission\" as the latter focus will take on forever to integrate and finally form Gansu Ma as the ⟦1⟧.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "193rgu3",
   "en": "Japan"
  },
  {
   "k": "4pkj1y",
   "en": "Xibei San Ma"
  },
  {
   "k": "xirak8",
   "en": "If the player wants to do the other part, make sure you prepare yourself to fight Sinkiang, the player only has to worry about ⟦0⟧ as to take down and annex Sinkiang, in order to go as far as unite all of China. Fighting the Ma's can be relatively tedious. Gansu Ma and Khotan Ma being relatively easy to take down with the outmanoeuvring strategy. And Qinghai Ma would be a decent difficulty as they have more territory (despite being known as the original Xibei San Ma). If the player has finally taken Gansu Ma, go for Khotan Ma, first and then Qinghai Ma second. Khotan Ma falls weak and defeated against the looming war with Sinkiang, so if the player wishes to incorporate cores faster, then Khotan Ma has to go first. Finally with Qinghai Ma last, by using the same outmanoeuvring and pin down attack strategies, Ningxia Ma can form Xibei San Ma. With this done and if the player has completed all of the warlord focuses of Ningxia Ma, it is time to rush and go for Warlord subjugation in the generic Nationalist China focus tree. It would give a few wargoals for the player to strike and annex the warlords. Alternatively, go with the \"Invite Foreign Investors\" by rushing down all the way until you reach the \"One China Policy\".",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "1wkqlu",
   "en": "Considering that the \"Renegotiate the Unequal Treaties\" focus is usually bypassed as Xibei San Ma doesnt have the national spirit. If China and the rest of the East sided warlords are at war with Japan, it is a good opportunity to pick targets one by one. Be vary of the territories. Of the said nations. The Northeastern Army, in comparison to Sichuan and Communist China, is an easier target. Whereas the other two tend to increase their army, and utilize their mountainous terrain. In alternative to that, use the border conflict decision missions as an alternative to gain territory against the neighbors. Make sure to fix the supply routes, research trains and improve on division templates. Otherwise, if that proves to be obsolete, simply declare war on them by \"One China Policy\" focus, battle them in a preferable terrain. Or, research mountaineer divisions to fare better in the mountainous battlefields."
  },
  {
   "k": "vg2aji",
   "en": "In addition, Ningxia Ma can ironically become the second most industrial power in China, only behind Chiang's ⟦0⟧, thanks due to both its Warlord and Ma Clique shared focus trees.",
   "frags": 1
  },
